: one identity contract, one transmission gate, snapshot-bound discard, verified outcomes\n\nStructural correction for independent review 39244 (R10 head 4a37173 / 8f3d316;\nD1-D7, P3), not per-witness patches:\n\n- resolveIdentity: the only way any stored copy (IndexedDB record, v2, aura_q3,\n  aura_q4) gets a lifecycle identity -- from storage context (key/record account,\n  outer id incl. missing/malformed index, incomplete aura_q4 keys) plus nested\n  identity, never the signed-in account. valid | damaged | incomplete |\n  contradictory; only valid is sendable, valid+damaged are discarded durably,\n  incomplete/contradictory are preserved and block every candidate id. A value\n  naming another account is a contradiction, no longer skipped (D3); a missing\n  outer id no longer hides a nested identity (D1); an incomplete aura_q4 key is\n  never trusted (D7).\n- eligibilityGate: the same check, over every copy of the account, inside the\n  claiming transaction for direct submission and replay (D2).\n- discardOwned: bound to the confirmed snapshot's identities, re-resolved in the\n  transaction (D4); a fresh claim keeps the whole logical activity (D5); the\n  decision keeps the prior-send fact across cleanup retries (D6); an unconfirmed\n  commit is verified by a separate read -> cleanup-pending / failed / uncertain,\n  never an assumed rollback (P3). One send is attributed once.\n- Sign-out messages: no claims about later syncing or \"never sent\" for kept or\n  unidentified copies; uncertain outcome reported.\n\nReviewer disposition, probes and logs preserved (docs/android/evidence/\nrel04-r10-independent-39244, SHA256SUMS); test/rel04R11StructuralQueue reproduces\nevery witness on vendored 8f3d316 and adds the cross-format matrix. No historical\nassertion changed. No new format, migration, marker expiry or worker change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-11-26T17:45:02Z","author":{"name":"Stephen Francis","email":"steve